  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration so far is config_005 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) at 0.650 acc, while the image-only model (config_010, resnet50, singleprofile) is very weak at 0.208 acc. We have strong evidence about which RNA encoder, profile setting, and aggregation work best, but zero evidence on whether the image modality adds any value when fused with a strong RNA representation. Question: config_030 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, concat) directly tests whether adding resnet50 image features via the simplest fusion (concat) to the best-known RNA pipeline improves or degrades performance. Why best: This is the central hypothesis of a multimodal cellular profiling study. The answer determines whether the remaining budget should be spent exploring multimodal variants (weighted fusion, ViT, transformer aggregation) or focused on refining the RNA-only pipeline. It uses the best-validated RNA settings, so any performance change can be attributed to the addition of the image modality and fusion, making it a clean, high-information experiment under the limited budget."
